---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Resume — Ian West" description="Ian West's resume — full-stack .NET and React engineer based in Columbus, OH.">
  <div class="resume-header">
    <h1>Resume</h1>
    <a href="/ian-west-resume.pdf" download class="download-btn">
      <svg aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4" />
        <polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10" />
        <line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3" />
      </svg>
      Download PDF
    </a>
  </div>

  <p class="summary">Full-stack software engineer specializing in .NET and React, with deep experience taking a single-tenant application to a multi-tenant SaaS platform on Azure. Owns features from infrastructure and API to data model and UI, and builds the integrations that connect a product to the outside world. Diplomatic, personable, and driven to solve human problems.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Technical Skills</h2>
    <dl class="skills">
      <dt>Languages</dt>
      <dd>C#, TypeScript, JavaScript, SQL (T-SQL), Java, Python, Bash</dd>
      <dt>Backend</dt>
      <dd>.NET 10, ASP.NET Core, .NET Aspire, EF Core, REST APIs, clean/onion architecture, Spring Boot</dd>
      <dt>Frontend</dt>
      <dd>React, Redux Toolkit / RTK Query, React Hook Form, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Node</dd>
      <dt>Data</dt>
      <dd>MS SQL Server, PostgreSQL, Redis, EF Core migrations, query optimization and SQL projections</dd>
      <dt>Cloud &amp; DevOps</dt>
      <dd>Azure (Container Apps, App Service, SQL, Key Vault, Front Door, Entra ID, App Insights), Terraform, Bicep, Docker, GitHub Actions, CI/CD, per-PR preview deployments, blue/green deploys</dd>
      <dt>Testing</dt>
      <dd>Vitest, Playwright, xUnit, Jest, unit and integration testing</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Experience</h2>

    <div class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <div>
          <h3>BBI Logistics</h3>
          <span class="org">Columbus, OH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="date">Jan 2023 – Present</span>
      </div>

      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <h4>Senior Software Engineer</h4>
          <span class="date">Apr 2026 – Present</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Architected the migration of BBI's Transportation Management System (TMS) from a single-tenant application to a multi-tenant SaaS platform, so provisioning a tenant is a config file and a few pipeline runs, not an engineering project. One Terraform module gives each tenant an isolated Azure stack, and users sign in through their own company's Entra ID.</li>
          <li>Co-designed a multi-tenant integration service that authenticates and translates partner webhooks before they reach the TMS, 3M+ requests a month; built 11 of its 15 integrations across freight marketplaces, tracking networks, accounting, payments, and phone systems.</li>
          <li>Solely designed and built the EDI platform (X12 via Orderful) that processes 400K+ transactions a month for 20+ trading partners, including Fortune 500 shippers, and auto-builds 1,800+ loads a month from inbound tenders. Partners plug into a stable core pipeline as mappers; three teammates have since onboarded new customers that way.</li>
          <li>Established the delivery model behind 70+ production deploys a month: Terraform for all infrastructure, trunk-based development with per-PR preview deployments, one immutable image per merge promoted to production, and pipeline-applied migrations. Added distributed tracing across the TMS, integration, and EDI services, so a failed partner transaction traces from webhook to database in one place.</li>
          <li>Designed and built automated track and trace from an operations-written process spec, monitoring 3,000+ in-transit loads a month. When a truck's electronic logging device (ELD) goes dark, the system texts the driver for a location, keeps customer tracking feeds current, and escalates to operations only when automation can't recover. It tells one dark truck from a provider-wide outage and holds driver texts during the latter.</li>
          <li>Set the team's architecture, testing, and API conventions, and packaged its runbooks (EDI onboarding, cross-service debugging, triage, release notes) as shared Claude Code skills, alongside AI code review in CI.</li>
          <li>Mentor interns and junior developers, guiding coding practices and supporting their technical growth.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="role">
        <div class="role-header">
          <h4>Software Engineer</h4>
          <span class="date">Jan 2023 – Apr 2026</span>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Product Owner of the BBI Transportation TMS, defining requirements with stakeholders and leading feature work.</li>
          <li>As 1 of 4 developers, designed and built a full-stack TMS contributing to $4M+ in annual revenue.</li>
          <li>Built a .NET API for QuickBooks integration and a CI/CD pipeline automating build, test, deployment, and rollback.</li>
          <li>Pioneered frontend testing with Vitest and Playwright and wrote the documentation now shared across teams.</li>
          <li>Developed customer- and carrier-facing portals with real-time freight status, and a live company stats dashboard in React.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <div>
          <h3>Mechanic</h3>
          <span class="org">Paradise Garage, Columbus, OH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="date">Apr 2020 – Sep 2022</span>
      </div>
      <p class="desc">Learned bicycle repair from no experience and was promoted to full-time mechanic in under 12 months.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <div>
          <h3>Barista</h3>
          <span class="org">Fox in the Snow, Columbus, OH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="date">Jul 2018 – Aug 2020</span>
      </div>
      <p class="desc">Delivered hospitality at the highest-grossing cafe in the business, coordinating with a team of 12+.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <div>
          <h3>Lead Coffee Roaster</h3>
          <span class="org">Mission Coffee Co, Columbus, OH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="date">Apr 2017 – Jul 2018</span>
      </div>
      <p class="desc">Roasted specialty-grade coffee with Cropster and sense-based methods; promoted from barista within 12 months.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Education</h2>

    <div class="entry">
      <div class="entry-header">
        <div>
          <h3>Tech Elevator</h3>
          <span class="org">Columbus, OH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="date">Sep 2022 – Dec 2022</span>
      </div>
      <p class="desc">14-week full-stack coding bootcamp: 800+ hours building dynamic web-based software systems in Java.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .resume-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .resume-header h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .download-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .download-btn:hover {
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .summary {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  section > h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .skills {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .skills dt {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .skills dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .skills {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }

    .skills dd {
      margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    }
  }

  .entry {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .entry-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .entry-header h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .role {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .role-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .role-header h4 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .org {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .date {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .desc {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
